    "summary": "Portrait of a man; single-page painting mounted on album folio. Man wearing a pale blue robe lined with red and green floral patterned material over a red-orange skirt. Wide, thick red, yellow and white waistband with a Khanjar tucked into it and a pearl-encrusted amulet suspended from it. He wears a tall black hat with pearl and feather decoration. In his right hand is an orange (or other fruit). Album contains 19 paintings of Persian costumes.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album bound in green leather with gold gilt trim, with pages of gold trim. Includes loose letter (in French) on thin blue paper describing contents and addressed to recipient.",
